\# SLICYWEB SMART SLICER



\# CLAUDE PROJECT CONTEXT



Version: 1.0.0



Status: Approved



Priority: High



\---



\# Project Overview



Project Name:



SlicyWeb Smart Slicer



Project Type:



AI-Assisted 3D Printing Preparation Software



Purpose:



Provide intelligent print preparation, analysis, recommendations, and optimization for 3D printing workflows.



The application focuses on:



\- Visualization

\- Analysis

\- Recommendations

\- Optimization

\- Print Preparation



The initial versions do not generate G-Code.



\---



\# Core Goals



The software must:



\- Import STL files

\- Import 3MF files

\- Open WYPROJ projects

\- Save WYPROJ projects

\- Analyze 3D models

\- Recommend print settings

\- Detect print risks

\- Estimate print duration

\- Estimate print cost

\- Optimize object orientation

\- Assist users with reliable printing decisions



\---



\# Supported Formats



Import Formats:



\- STL

\- 3MF

\- WYPROJ



Native Project Format:



\- WYPROJ



Project Extension:



\- .wyproj



Internal Storage Format:



\- JSON



Project files must remain versioned and compatible.



\---



\# Technology Stack



Frontend:



\- React

\- TypeScript



Desktop Framework:



\- Electron



3D Engine:



\- Three.js



State Management:



\- Zustand



\---



\# Architecture



Application Flow:



GUI

↓

Service

↓

Repository

↓

RepositorySync

↓

Remote Source



Repository access must remain centralized.



Direct repository access from GUI is prohibited.



Business logic must remain outside GUI components.



\---



\# AI System



The recommendation system is:



\- Rule Based

\- Deterministic

\- Reproducible



Recommendations are generated using:



\- Printer Profiles

\- Material Profiles

\- Filament Profiles

\- Model Analysis

\- Object Classification



The AI must never invent:



\- Printer capabilities

\- Material limits

\- Filament properties

\- Recommendations unsupported by available data



Unknown values must be treated as unknown.



\---



\# Development Principles



The project follows:



\- Documentation First

\- Impact Analysis First

\- Patch First

\- Compatibility First

\- Domain Ownership

\- Dependency Governance

\- Architecture Protection



Preferred strategy:



1\. Analyze

2\. Verify Ownership

3\. Verify Dependencies

4\. Perform Impact Analysis

5\. Modify

6\. Validate

7\. Update Documentation

8\. Verify Consistency



Large rewrites are prohibited unless explicitly approved.



\---



\# Governance Principles



Documentation is the Source Of Truth.



Implementation must follow documentation.



Changes require:



\- Ownership Verification

\- Dependency Verification

\- Impact Analysis

\- Documentation Review

\- Compatibility Verification



Governance and documentation consistency are mandatory.



\---



\# Internationalization



The application must support multilingual user interfaces.



Initial languages:



\- English

\- French

\- Hebrew



Additional languages may be added in future releases.



Requirements:



\- User-facing text must support localization.

\- GUI text should not be hardcoded.

\- Architecture should remain language-independent.

\- WYPROJ project files must remain language-neutral.



\---



\# Project Priorities



Priority Order:



1\. Stability

2\. Compatibility

3\. Reliability

4\. Safety

5\. Quality

6\. Performance

7\. New Features



A working feature must never be broken to add a new feature.



